WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:11.034
Hi! The flowers, the birds and all of us depend on water. Today let's see how living things use water, and how we can protect it.

2
00:00:11.184 --> 00:00:16.314
All living things need water. Without water, they cannot survive.

3
00:00:16.464 --> 00:00:24.522
Plants use water to make food. Water also keeps plants firm. A plant without enough water wilts and droops.

4
00:00:24.672 --> 00:00:32.442
Our bodies use water to help digest food. Blood is mostly water, and it carries nutrients around the body.

5
00:00:32.592 --> 00:00:40.482
When it's hot, we sweat. As the sweat evaporates, it takes heat away and cools the body down.

6
00:00:40.632 --> 00:00:49.602
But people sometimes make water dirty. This is called water pollution. One example is throwing rubbish into rivers and seas.

7
00:00:49.752 --> 00:00:56.562
When ships spill oil, it floats on the water. It sticks birds' feathers together and makes fish sick.

8
00:00:56.712 --> 00:01:03.714
When factories pour harmful chemicals and waste water into rivers, the living things in the water can die.

9
00:01:03.864 --> 00:01:11.754
Water pollution harms living things, and it also means there is less clean fresh water for us to use.

10
00:01:11.904 --> 00:01:23.850
Singapore is small, so fresh water is precious. Singapore has Four National Taps. The first is local catchment: rainwater is collected and stored in reservoirs.

11
00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:26.754
The second is imported water.

12
00:01:26.904 --> 00:01:32.178
The third is NEWater: used water is treated until it is very clean.

13
00:01:32.328 --> 00:01:39.522
The fourth is desalinated water: salt is removed from sea water to make fresh water.

14
00:01:39.672 --> 00:01:44.154
Each of us can help save water. Take shorter showers.

15
00:01:44.304 --> 00:01:48.474
Turn off the tap while you brush your teeth or soap your hands.

16
00:01:48.624 --> 00:01:53.394
If you see a leaking tap, tell an adult so it can be fixed quickly.

17
00:01:53.544 --> 00:01:59.610
Water used to wash vegetables or rice can be reused to water plants.

18
00:01:59.760 --> 00:02:07.314
Watch out! Some people say there's so much water on Earth that we never need to save it. That's not true!

19
00:02:07.464 --> 00:02:14.538
Most water on Earth is salty sea water. Only a small part is clean fresh water we can use.

20
00:02:14.688 --> 00:02:22.482
Pollution and waste both reduce the water we can use, so we must save water and keep it clean.

21
00:02:22.632 --> 00:02:31.674
Your turn! What happens to a plant that doesn't get enough water? Pause and think.

22
00:02:31.824 --> 00:02:38.226
It wilts and droops, and it can't make food properly. Did you get it right?

23
00:02:38.376 --> 00:02:46.794
Another one! Name two ways to save water. Pause and think.

24
00:02:46.944 --> 00:02:57.450
For example: turn off the tap while brushing, reuse vegetable-washing water on plants, or take shorter showers. Did you get it right?

25
00:02:57.600 --> 00:03:06.306
Last one! Where does Singapore's NEWater come from? Pause and think.

26
00:03:06.456 --> 00:03:13.986
NEWater is used water that has been treated until it is very clean. Did you get it right?

27
00:03:14.136 --> 00:03:26.322
Remember: all living things need water. Pollution harms living things, and waste means less fresh water. Singapore has Four National Taps, and every one of us can save water.

28
00:03:26.472 --> 00:03:31.746
When you brush your teeth today, remember to turn off the tap!

